# The core helper files internal/corecopy/ holds (tools/corecopy.sh): globs
# relative to the core's internal/, test files never copied. The list starts
# from what the code moved here imports; the commit that moves it completes
# it from `go list` of that code.
#
# Whole files only, so what lives in a file of its own is copied and the
# rest is not: auth.User sits in auth/store.go beside the store (bcrypt, the
# core's users table, the app tokens), the channels types (Rules, ExtraTitle,
# Stream, ExtrasOn) in channels/store.go and extras.go beside the Service
# and the Builder, library/visibility.go is methods of the Repo, and the
# progress and tracking stores need the core's database. The addon takes
# the profile from addonkit (online.User is addonkit.User), the channel
# types from addonkit's channels.* hook types (online.Stream is its own),
# the library, the progress and the profiles from *addonkit.Client (the
# interfaces of online/progress.go and channels.go), the tracked titles'
# sources through coreadapt.Tracking, and its watched states and scanner
# types are online's own. media.LiveInput (the loopback rule of ffmpeg's
# input) is checked by hand in the channel test.

# i18n: the machinery and the genre keys (the addon's own English catalog
# is its own)
i18n/i18n.go i18n/catalog.go i18n/genres.go
# the library model and the rating rules (RatingAllowed), without the Repo
# and the Service, which need the core's database
library/model.go library/errors.go library/rating.go
# the image cache's file names (online's posters)
library/image_url.go
# the TMDB client (genres: its cache) and discover, without the library
# enrichers (enrich.go, photos.go and translations.go work on library.Repo),
# and the metadata helpers the client builds on (raw URLs, the JSON fetch)
metadata/httpjson.go metadata/raw.go metadata/ratelimit.go
metadata/tmdb/client.go metadata/tmdb/genres.go metadata/tmdb/discover.go
# only the sidecar and conversion helpers of the subtitles package (Decode,
# NormLang, SniffLang): the client needs auto.go and the core's database
subtitles/sidecar.go
# the SQLite snapshot the one-time import reads
sqlitesnap/*.go
# the tracked titles' model without the core's Service and Store
tracking/model.go
